---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Read the High in the FlightSim Sky privacy policy, including how YouTube API data, local storage preferences, and third-party services are handled on this site."
>
  <div class="policy-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    
    <section>
      <h2>Introduction</h2>
      <p>
        High in the FlightSim Sky ("we", "our", or "us") operates the website. This page
        informs you of our policies regarding the collection, use, and
        disclosure of personal data when you use our Service and the choices
        you have associated with that data.
      </p>
      <p>
        This website uses YouTube API Services and embedded YouTube players to
        display channel videos, playlists, and related content.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>YouTube API Services Disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        In addition to our own privacy procedures, we utilize YouTube API
        Services. Users can learn more about how Google manages data by
        visiting the <a href="https://www.google.com/policies/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        By using this website, you may interact with YouTube content and
        services that are governed by the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">YouTube Terms of Service</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Data Collection and Processing</h2>
      <p>
        Our website is a static site hosted on GitHub Pages. We do not collect
        personal information directly. However:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>YouTube content metadata:</strong> We use YouTube API Services
          to retrieve and display public channel information such as video
          titles, video IDs, descriptions, thumbnails, publication dates, view
          counts, playlists, and live-status information.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>How we use that data:</strong> We use this information only to
          build and display the public pages of this website, including video
          archives, playlists, embeds, search, and related content discovery.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>How we share that data:</strong> We do not sell or share
          YouTube API data with external parties for independent marketing or
          analytics purposes. The content is displayed on this public website,
          hosted on GitHub Pages, and embedded video playback is provided by
          YouTube.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>User data from YouTube interactions:</strong> We do not
          collect or store personal information from visitors through YouTube
          API Services. However, when you load pages containing embedded
          YouTube players or YouTube-linked content, Google or YouTube may
          receive technical data such as your IP address, browser information,
          and interaction data as part of normal service operation.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>GitHub Pages:</strong> Hosting is provided by GitHub. Review
          GitHub's privacy policy for hosting-related data practices.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Third-party Analytics:</strong> If implemented, we use
          analytics services to understand usage patterns.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Contact Form:</strong> If enabled, form submissions are
          processed by a third-party form provider. Data you submit (such as
          name, email, and message) is handled according to that provider's
          privacy policy.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
      <p>
        Our website does not set any cookies. We do not use tracking cookies.
        Embedded YouTube players and other external services may set their own
        cookies subject to their own policies.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use your browser's built-in <strong>localStorage</strong> and
        <strong>sessionStorage</strong> to save preferences on your device only.
        This data is never transmitted to our servers. Specifically:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Theme preference</strong> (<code>theme</code>): Stores your
          light/dark mode choice so it persists across visits.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Favourite videos</strong> (<code>fav-videos</code>) and
          <strong>favourite controller configs</strong> (<code>fav-configs</code>):
          Stores the IDs of items you have bookmarked on the Favourites page.
          This data stays on your device and is cleared if you clear your
          browser data or use the "Clear all favourites" button on that page.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Learning Track progress</strong>: Stores lesson completion
          state per track so your progress is remembered between visits.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Live banner dismissal</strong>: Uses sessionStorage to
          remember that you have dismissed the live stream notification banner
          for the current browser session. This clears automatically when you
          close the tab.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>External Links</h2>
      <p>
        Our website may contain links to external sites (YouTube, GitHub, etc.).
        This Privacy Policy does not apply to external websites. We encourage
        you to review their privacy policies.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use HTTPS encryption to protect your connection to our site. However,
        no method of transmission over the internet is 100% secure.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update our Privacy Policy from time to time. Changes will be
        posted on this page with an updated "Last Modified" date.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, our use of YouTube API
        Services, or your data, please use our <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can also open an issue on our GitHub repository if your request is
        appropriate for a public discussion.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p><strong>Last Modified:</strong> May 2026</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy-page {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 2rem 1rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .policy-page h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    color: var(--text-heading);
  }

  .policy-page h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-heading);
  }

  .policy-page section {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .policy-page p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .policy-page a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .policy-page a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .policy-page ul {
    margin: 1rem 0;
    padding-left: 2rem;
  }

  .policy-page li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  strong {
    color: var(--text-heading);
  }
</style>
